## Ring Settings for a 1.5 Carat Emerald Cut Diamond

[![1.5 carat emerald cut diamond ring in 18K white gold solitaire setting — clean rectangular step-cut outline](/images/505033_M1_EMR_DIM_wht_0100CT_W_Box4_004_1600X1600.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?MetalType=all&Diamonds=Dia&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

At 1.5ct and 8.0mm × 6.0mm, the emerald cut stone has real presence. The setting needs to frame the rectangle — not fight it. A pavé band works well here in a way it doesn't at 1ct: the 8mm stone is large enough to anchor shoulder sparkle without being overshadowed by it.

Avoid round halo settings. They put a circular border around a clean rectangle. The stone reads smaller inside the halo because your eye expects a circle to follow the curve — the emerald cut's hard right angles break that expectation and create visual noise instead of elegance.

