The [$690 Petite Solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/petite-emerald-cut-solitaire-diamond-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-311196?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is purpose-built for the emerald cut shape. Prong placement is matched to the stone's corners — that matters more at 1.5ct than at smaller sizes because the four corners of an 8mm stone are more exposed to everyday impact.

The [$1,515 Riviera Pavé](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/riviera-pave-diamond-band-engagement-ring-in-18k-white-gold-item-195326?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the best upgrade at this size. At 1.5ct, the center stone is large enough to carry shoulder sparkle without being visually competed by it. The 478 review count confirms this is a proven combination.

> "At 1.5ct, I lean toward the Riviera Pavé over a plain solitaire. The stone is large enough to anchor it. The shoulder sparkle from the pavé band adds to the step-cut's long light flashes rather than competing with them. You get a ring that reads as both elegant and substantial without the price of a bezel." — Farzana, diamond advisor

---

## The $10K Clarity Wall

This is the most important rule for a natural 1.5ct emerald cut buyer.

At 1ct, the emerald cut table is 6.5mm wide. An SI1 inclusion at 6.5mm is borderline — placement determines whether it shows. At 1.5ct, the table expands to 8.0mm.

At 8mm, an SI1 inclusion anywhere near the center of the table is visible to the naked eye at arm's length. No video trick, no photograph angle, no lighting condition hides it. The step facets act as a magnifier, not a scatterer — everything in the stone is on display.

VS1 is the floor. Not VS2. Not SI1. VS1 — where inclusions are reliably microscopic and invisible under all normal viewing conditions.

[![Emerald cut solitaire in white gold — step facets showing at 1.5ct, clarity critical at this table width](/images/505031_M1_EMR_DIM_wht_0100CT_W_Box2_004_1600X1600.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?MetalType=all&Diamonds=Dia&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

The certified market agrees: all three natural 1.5ct emerald cuts in current inventory sit at VS1 or better. That is not coincidence. Stones below VS2 at this size fail in the market.

Buyers see inclusions face-up when viewing HD video — and return them. Certified retailers have stopped listing them at this size. The $10K Clarity Wall is the market's own ruling on the matter.

VS2 at 1.5ct is technically acceptable only if the GIA plot shows inclusions at the perimeter of the stone, away from the center table. That requires watching the stone's HD video before purchase. At $10,000+ committed to a stone, guessing on VS2 placement is the wrong call.

