The $10K Clarity Wall exists because VS1 is expensive at natural 1.5ct. There is no budget shortcut around it in natural diamonds. If VS1 at $10,409 is over budget, the answer is not to lower the clarity grade. The answer is to switch to lab — which is The 3ct Lab Leap, explained below.

---

## The 8mm Threshold — What 1.5ct Actually Looks Like on the Hand

At 1.5ct, an emerald cut diamond measures approximately 8.0mm long by 6.0mm wide. This is a significant step up from the 1ct stone at 6.5mm × 5.0mm — 1.5mm longer, 1.0mm wider, and visually in a different category.

The 8mm length is The 8mm Threshold: the size at which the hall-of-mirrors effect is fully visible from arm's length. At 1ct (6.5mm), the step-cut corridors are short and the effect is developing. At 1.5ct (8mm), the long step facets have enough physical length to build deep parallel light reflections.

A friend standing across a dinner table can see the hall-of-mirrors working. That does not happen at 1ct — the table is simply too short to carry the effect that far. The extra 1.5mm in length is not a small upgrade; it crosses a threshold.

This is why 1.5ct is such a common choice for buyers who specifically want the emerald cut's optical character rather than just carat weight. The shape only fully delivers its signature look at The 8mm Threshold and above.

