The ideal L/W ratio at 1.5ct is 1.28–1.40. Below 1.25, the stone looks nearly square — the emerald cut's elongated character disappears. Above 1.45, it reads as a very narrow sliver, which looks unbalanced in most settings.

The [GIA E-VS1 at $10,409](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29298663?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is listed at 1.50ct. Confirm the exact L/W ratio on the GIA certificate before purchasing — two stones at 1.50ct can have meaningfully different face-up appearances depending on proportions.

