The natural 1.5ct ring at minimum spend is $11,099. The lab 3ct D-IF ring is $10,350 complete. The lab ring is larger, cleaner in grade, and $749 cheaper. The only argument for natural is origin — the stone came from the earth, not a reactor. That argument is real and valid for many buyers. But it is the only argument. On any other metric — size, clarity grade, price — the lab path wins at this budget.

